  "pp_id": "PP-13843305",
  "development_type": "Other advertisements",
  "description": "APPLICATION FOR ADVERTISEMENT CONSENT FOR THE INSTALLATION OF REPLACEMENT SIGN TO INCLUDE. 1X EXISTING CAR PARK ENTRANCE SIGN TO BE RELOCATED, 2 X SETS OF EXISTING HOUSE NAME LETTERS TO BE REFURBISHED AND RELOCATED, 1X SET OF INDIVIDUAL EXTERNALLY ILLUMINATED HOME OF THE ROAST LETTERS FITTED ON RUNNER BARS, 2X EXTERNALLY ILLUMINATED TOBY CARVERY SIGNS ",
  "site_name": null,
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed installation of large, illuminated lettering and logos by reason of its scale, design, illumination and quantum would appear incongruous and visually cluttered detracting from the external appearance of the Grade II Park Place listed building and it's setting and to the surrounding character and appearance of Mitcham Cricket Green Conservation Area contrary to Planning (Listed Buildings and Conservation Areas) Act 1990, Chapter 16 of the NPPF 2024, HC1 of the London Plan 2021 and D12.2, D12.3, D12.4, D12.5, Merton Local Plan 2024.",
    "Reason : 2 - INFORMATIVE\r\nNote to Applicant\r\nIn accordance with paragraph 38 of the NPPF, The London Borough of Merton  (LBM) takes a positive and proactive approach to development proposals focused on solutions. LBM works with applicants/agents in a positive and proactive manner by:\r\n\"\tOffering a pre-application advice and duty desk service. \r\n\"\tWhere possible, suggesting solutions to secure a successful outcome.\r\n\"\tAs appropriate, updating applicants/agents of any issues that may arise in the processing of their application.\r\nIn this instance:\r\n\"\tThe application was considered to be fundamentally contrary to the provisions of the Development Plan and the NPPF, and there were not considered to be any solutions to resolve this conflict. \r\n\"\tIt is noted that the applicant/agent did not engage in any pre-application discussions.\r\n\"\tThe applicant is advised to seek pre-application advice on any resubmission.\r\n"
  ],
